WITH q AS (
    INSERT INTO challenge.questions (challenge_id, question, type, explanation, order_index, points)
    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_gcn_171'), 'The deployment sets `terminationGracePeriodSeconds: 30`. A stuck report export kept the gateway''s `Shutdown` waiting:

```text
10:04:00  SIGTERM received, draining
10:04:05  listener closed, waiting for 1 request
10:04:30  (pod gone)
$ kubectl -n rice-rocket get events --field-selector involvedObject.name=gateway-7c9f
Normal  Killing  pod/gateway-7c9f  Stopping container gateway
```

Statement: "When the 30 seconds run out, the kubelet sends SIGTERM a second time and waits another grace period, so a shutdown that takes 45 seconds still finishes cleanly."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. When the grace period ends and the container is still running, the kubelet sends SIGKILL: no handler runs, buffered logs are lost and the workers stop mid-job. The shutdown must fit inside the grace period with a margin, which is why the `Shutdown` context gets a budget (grace period minus the drain delay, the time to stop the workers and a margin), and a request that would overrun it is cut on purpose. The misconception is that the grace period is a polite reminder.', 3, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_gcn_171') AND order_index = 3)
    RETURNING id
)
