```go
requestSeconds.WithLabelValues(r.URL.Path).Observe(elapsed.Seconds())
```

```text
$ curl -s localhost:9090/metrics | grep -c ''gateway_request_seconds_bucket{path="/orders/''
183644
```

Statement: "This is fine: Prometheus compresses repeated label values, so one series per order id costs almost nothing."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. Every distinct label value creates a separate time series, with its own buckets (8 series per histogram here), its own index entries and its own memory in the gateway and in Prometheus; label values are not deduplicated into one series. Order ids are unbounded, so the series count grows with business volume until scrapes slow down and queries time out. Label with the route template (`/orders/{id}`, or `r.Pattern` in Go 1.23+) and put ids in logs or traces instead. The misconception is that labels are cheap metadata.', 2, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_gcn_181') AND order_index = 2)
    RETURNING id
)
