```go
log := slog.New(slog.NewJSONHandler(os.Stdout, nil)).With("request_id", rid, "route", "/checkout")
log.Info("payment call", "provider", "momo", "ms", 2870)
```

```text
{"time":"2026-11-06T11:42:07Z","level":"INFO","msg":"payment call","request_id":"8f3a1c","route":"/checkout","provider":"momo","ms":2870}
```

Statement: "`With` returns a logger that adds `request_id` and `route` to every line written through it, so all lines of one slow checkout can be found with one query on `request_id`."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. `Logger.With` returns a new logger carrying those attributes, and the JSON handler writes them as fields on every record, so a log query on `request_id="8f3a1c"` returns the whole story of that request (here: a 2.87 s call to the payment provider). Structured fields replace parsing free text with regular expressions. The misconception is that attributes have to be repeated on each log call.', 3, 5
